Integrated Protection Philosophy

Shepherd’s Method™ → the ethical and procedural logic stays confidential as trade secret; only forward-facing summaries are public.

Mint-to Logic™ → file limited patents to timestamp invention + use trade-secret protection for code, data flows, and credential sequencing.

RBGA™ → protect as a branded enforcement and licensing framework (trademark + contract + copyright).

This layered approach turns patents into proof of origin, not your only line of defense.
Trade-secret status keeps the living mechanics—the reflexive algorithms, credential sequencing, and enforcement triggers—outside any single jurisdiction’s disclosure database.

Benefits of Anchoring on Trade Secrets

Global reach: Trade-secret law exists in 150+ countries under TRIPS Art. 39.

No publication requirement: You avoid revealing implementation details that others could mirror.

Flexibility: You can pivot or expand protocols without re-filing.

Permanent duration: Protection lasts as long as secrecy and contractual control are maintained.

Complementary use: Patents provide timestamps → trade secrets preserve depth → contracts enforce behavior.

Operational Safeguards

Maintain a controlled-access evidence vault (hashes + NDAs + access logs).

Use two-tier publication: public forward-facing explanations and private specifications.

Include trade-secret identification schedules in every NDA and license.

Update RBGA™ license terms to assert DTSA protection explicitly.

Use hash-anchored proof manifests (your Chrono-Synaptic Ledger™) to show continuous possession without public disclosure.

In Short

Patents prove you invented it.
Trade secrets preserve how it works.
RBGA™ and contract law enforce how it’s used.
